---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Sergi Romero"
  description="About Sergi Romero: robotics and automation engineer working at the intersection of robotics, software, and intelligent systems."
>
  <main class="about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <section aria-labelledby="profile-heading">
      <h2 id="profile-heading">Profile</h2>
      <p>
        I’m a robotics and automation engineer interested in building intelligent
        systems at the intersection of robotics, software, and machine learning.
        My interests include artificial intelligence, neural networks, perception,
        control, and research.
      </p>
      <p>
        I particularly enjoy working on problems where software meets the physical
        world — designing systems that combine sensing, control, communication,
        and data-driven methods. I also care about understanding and communicating
        the engineering decisions behind the systems I build.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="education-heading">
      <h2 id="education-heading">Education</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>M.Sc. in Robotics and Automatic Control</strong> —
          Universitat Politècnica de Catalunya (UPC), ETSEIB
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>B.Sc. in Industrial Electronic Engineering and Electronics</strong> —
          Universitat Politècnica de Catalunya (UPC), EEBE
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
      <h2 id="experience-heading">Experience</h2>

      <div class="job">
        <h3>Universal Robots (UR) — R&amp;D Software, Student Worker</h3>
        <p class="job-meta">Odense, Denmark · Master's internship · ~6 months</p>

        <p>
          I worked in the R&amp;D team responsible for software used to interface
          with and control Universal Robots. My work focused on the external
          control and communication stack, contributing to both existing
          open-source components and new software developed from scratch.
        </p>

        <p>
          One of my main projects was the official
          <a
            href="https://github.com/UniversalRobots/RTDE_ROS2_Publisher"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >RTDE_ROS2_Publisher</a>
          package, which I developed from scratch. I also contributed to the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Universal Robots Client Library</a>
          and the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_ROS2_Driver"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Universal Robots ROS 2 Driver</a>.
        </p>

        <p>Some of the areas I worked on include:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>URScript &amp; external control</strong> — developing and
            working with robot-side scripts and the real-time communication
            setup used for external control.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>RTDE</strong> — working with Universal Robots' Real-Time Data
            Exchange protocol and developing the RTDE_ROS2_Publisher package.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>UR Caps &amp; Angular</strong> — designing a UR Cap,
            a front-end extension running directly on the robot's teach pendant.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Client library &amp; ROS 2 driver</strong> — contributing to
            socket communication, multithreading, real-time scheduling (FIFO),
            payload handling, and tool communication.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Testing &amp; software quality</strong> — writing unit and
            integration tests, improving CI workflows, and debugging issues
            across the software stack.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="note">
          My open-source work from this internship is available on
          <a
            href="https://github.com/srvald"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >GitHub</a>,
          including merged contributions to the Universal Robots ROS ecosystem.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <h3>Mobile Industrial Robots (MiR) — Technical Engineer</h3>
        <p class="job-meta">Intern, then part-time · ~2 years</p>

        <p>
          I worked in technical service while completing my degree, gaining
          hands-on experience with both the hardware and software of autonomous
          mobile robots.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Hardware &amp; troubleshooting</strong> — diagnosing and
            repairing robots while developing an understanding of the physical
            systems behind them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>ROS &amp; networking</strong> — diagnosing software and
            communication issues using ROS topics, nodes, networking tools,
            and <code>rosout</code> logs.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>REST API</strong> — developing small applications and tools
            using the MiR REST API.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>